      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To determine the value of \\( n \\) that makes the four-digit number \\( 712n \\) divisible by 18, we need to check the divisibility rules for both 2 and 9. A number is divisible by 18 if and only if it is divisible by both 2 and 9.\n\n1. **Divisibility by 2**: A number is divisible by 2 if its last digit is even. Therefore, \\( n \\) must be one of the even digits, i.e., \\( n \\) can be 0, 2, 4, 6, or 8.\n2. **Divisibility by 9**: A number is divisible by 9 if the sum of its digits is divisible by 9. The sum of the digits of \\( 712n \\) is \\( 7 + 1 + 2 + n = 10 + n \\). So, \\( 10 + n \\) must be divisible by 9.\n\nNow, we will check which of the even digits \\( n \\) makes \\( 10 + n \\) divisible by 9.\n\n- If \\( n = 0 \\), then \\( 10 + 0 = 10 \\), which is not divisible by 9.\n- If \\( n = 2 \\), then \\( 10 + 2 = 12 \\), which is not divisible by 9.\n- If \\( n = 4 \\), then \\( 10 + 4 = 14 \\), which is not divisible by 9.\n- If \\( n = 6 \\), then \\( 10 + 6 = 16 \\), which is not divisible by 9.\n- If \\( n = 8 \\), then \\( 10 + 8 = 18 \\), which is divisible by 9.\n\nTherefore, the only value of \\( n \\) that satisfies both conditions (divisibility by 2 and divisibility by 9) is \\( n = 8 \\).\n\nThe final answer is \\(\\boxed{8}\\).",
